# Evening 1: First light
# An open meadow, only common fireflies, and the village close by.
# Learn to gather and carry.

name First light
length 180                  # seconds from sunset to full dark
critters 320 270 640 270    # where critter 1 and critter 2 start: x y x y
fireflies 12                # how many are out in the meadow at once
meadow 40 40 560 460        # where fireflies appear: x y width height
mix common 100              # chance of each kind: common, shy, pair

# The village, on the right. One line per lantern: x y
lantern 720 100
lantern 860 140
lantern 780 230
lantern 900 290
lantern 700 370
lantern 830 410
lantern 910 480
# Evening 2: Shy ones
# Shy fireflies dart away from critters. Brush past them from a distance,
# using the length of the string.

name Shy ones
critters 300 380 560 380
meadow 40 60 560 440
mix common 60 shy 40

# The village, up in the top-right corner.
lantern 700 90
lantern 820 70
lantern 920 130
lantern 760 190
lantern 880 240
lantern 720 300
lantern 900 360
# Evening 3: Partners
# Pair fireflies only cling when one sweep of the string touches both.
# This time the meadow is on the right and the village on the left.

name Partners
critters 420 270 680 270
meadow 380 40 540 460
mix common 50 shy 20 pair 30

# The village, on the left.
lantern 60 110
lantern 180 70
lantern 120 210
lantern 250 180
lantern 70 330
lantern 200 300
lantern 140 450
# Evening 4: The long way home
# A fence with two gaps and a few trees stand between the meadow and the
# village. Critters can't walk through them, and the string snags if it
# crosses one, so thread it through the gaps together.

name The long way home
critters 140 270 380 270
meadow 40 40 440 460
mix common 60 shy 20 pair 20

# The fence: three sections with gaps at y 150-230 and 340-420. (x y width height)
fence 560 0 16 150
fence 560 230 16 110
fence 560 420 16 120

# Trees on both sides of the fence. (x y radius)
tree 470 110 30
tree 480 440 26
tree 650 290 34
tree 660 480 24

# The village, beyond the fence.
lantern 760 90
lantern 880 150
lantern 790 230
lantern 910 300
lantern 760 380
lantern 870 430
lantern 920 500
# Evening 5: Breezy night
# Gusts blow from the village toward the meadow, pushing the critters and
# straining the string like a sail. Point the string into the wind and keep
# it short when a gust comes.

name Breezy night
critters 160 270 400 270
meadow 40 40 480 460
mix common 50 shy 25 pair 25
wind 90 180                 # strength (px/s) and direction in degrees (180 blows left)

# The village, upwind on the right.
lantern 700 120
lantern 830 80
lantern 900 200
lantern 760 260
lantern 880 340
lantern 720 420
lantern 850 470
# Evening 6: The footbridge
# A stream runs between the meadow and the village. Critters can't wade
# through it, and the only way across is a footbridge too narrow for two
# side by side, so cross single file. The string can pass over the water.

name The footbridge
critters 160 270 400 270
meadow 40 40 460 460
mix common 50 shy 25 pair 25

# The stream, in two parts with a 60-pixel gap between them. (x y width height)
water 560 0 80 240
water 560 300 80 240
# The bridge is drawn over the gap, a little wider than the stream.
bridge 548 240 104 60

# The village, across the stream.
lantern 720 100
lantern 860 90
lantern 790 200
lantern 910 260
lantern 730 330
lantern 850 400
lantern 750 470
# Evening 7: Festival night
# Everything at once: every kind of firefly, golden ones included, a fence
# and trees to thread through, and a light wind. Light the big lantern in
# the town square with a single delivery of at least 10 fireflies.

name Festival night
critters 140 270 360 270
fireflies 14
meadow 40 40 400 460
mix common 40 shy 25 pair 35
golden                      # golden fireflies appear when both critters stand still
wind 60 270                 # a light wind blowing up the screen

# A fence with two gaps between the meadow and the town.
fence 500 0 14 170
fence 500 250 14 60
fence 500 390 14 150

# Trees.
tree 440 460 24
tree 600 110 26
tree 610 450 26

# The town square: the big lantern (x y and the load it needs) and its ring.
biglantern 770 270 10
lantern 690 160
lantern 860 120
lantern 910 250
lantern 880 400
lantern 720 410
lantern 640 290
